01:10:14.400 --> 01:10:16.020
So that's how I met Randall.
所以我就是这样认识兰德尔的。

1326
01:10:16.160 --> 01:10:22.420
And it was a terrific, you know, added piece of the puzzle to start leaning into this reality
这真是太棒了，你知道，这是拼图中重要的一块，让我们开始倾向于这种

1327
01:10:22.420 --> 01:10:23.060
vibe.
真人秀的氛围。

1328
01:10:23.560 --> 01:10:25.640
I mean, it makes perfect sense that you say that.
我是说，你说得非常有道理。

1329
01:10:25.740 --> 01:10:29.960
I don't know why I haven't ever thought of it, but just the way we used to hold camcorders
我不知道为什么我从来没想过这一点，但我们过去拿摄像机的方式

1330
01:10:29.960 --> 01:10:32.000
is exactly the point of view.
正是那种视角。

1331
01:10:32.240 --> 01:10:32.380
Yeah.
没错。

1332
01:10:32.600 --> 01:10:33.840
And that's amazing.
这太神奇了。

1333
01:10:33.960 --> 01:10:35.160
I have never thought of that before.
我以前从来没想过这一点。

1334
01:10:35.420 --> 01:10:36.740
Yeah, it's slightly different with phones.
是啊，用手机拍稍微有点不同。

1335
01:10:36.960 --> 01:10:37.260
Yeah.
没错。

1336
01:10:37.380 --> 01:10:39.420
I think, at least the way I hold a phone.
至少我是这么拿手机的。

1337
01:10:39.600 --> 01:10:44.380
But if you're really good at phones, they have little handles and stuff and so the phone
但如果你很擅长用手机拍摄，它们有小手柄之类的东西，所以手机

1338
01:10:44.380 --> 01:10:45.400
doesn't wiggle around.
就不会晃来晃去。

1339
01:10:45.840 --> 01:10:46.080
Yeah.
没错。

1340
01:10:46.500 --> 01:10:46.740
Yeah.
没错。

1341
01:10:47.140 --> 01:10:51.360
Well, now you're working on the paper, but you finish shooting.
好吧，现在你在做后期，但你已经拍完了。

1342
01:10:51.820 --> 01:10:53.600
We finish shooting the first season.
我们拍完了第一季。

1343
01:10:53.600 --> 01:11:01.140
And we've, at the moment, at this point, we've locked picture on six of the first 10.
目前为止，前10集里我们已经锁定了6集的画面。

1344
01:11:01.420 --> 01:11:02.360
That's exciting.
那太令人兴奋了。

1345
01:11:04.360 --> 01:11:05.980
And it is exciting.
确实很令人兴奋。

1346
01:11:06.240 --> 01:11:13.020
And, you know, there's a lot of our old crew on the show, Kelly Cantley and Kasha Trojak
而且，你知道，我们剧组有很多老员工，凯莉·坎特利和卡莎·特罗亚克，

1347
01:11:13.020 --> 01:11:15.180
or the, you know, and Rusty Mahmood.
还有，你知道，拉斯蒂·马哈茂德。

1348
01:11:15.340 --> 01:11:18.320
They're all like the whole AD staff is the same guys.
他们都在，整个助理导演团队还是原来那些人。

1349
01:11:18.320 --> 01:11:21.180
And Sergio was catering it and, you know.
还有塞尔吉奥负责餐饮，你知道的。

1350
01:11:21.180 --> 01:11:22.060
You were so nice.
你真是太好了。

1351
01:11:22.060 --> 01:11:23.360
You invited us to set.
你邀请我们去片场。

1352
01:11:23.480 --> 01:11:24.820
We haven't shared about it yet.
我们还没分享过这件事。

1353
01:11:25.020 --> 01:11:29.820
But when we saw our crew, when we saw Sergio, we about lost our mind.
但当我们看到我们的剧组人员，看到塞尔吉奥（Sergio）时，我们简直要疯了。

1354
01:11:30.100 --> 01:11:30.240
Yeah.
没错。

1355
01:11:30.320 --> 01:11:32.160
And I was like, Sergio, do you still make your salsa?
我就问，塞尔吉奥，你还在做你的莎莎酱吗？

1356
01:11:32.320 --> 01:11:32.980
And he was like, yeah.
他说，还在做。

1357
01:11:33.560 --> 01:11:36.800
So, I mean, that was wonderful to see those faces.
所以，我是说，能看到那些面孔真是太棒了。

1358
01:11:37.420 --> 01:11:37.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1359
01:11:37.820 --> 01:11:40.100
It's very nice to have them around.
有他们在身边感觉真好。

1360
01:11:40.340 --> 01:11:41.320
And they keep you honeSt.
而且他们会让你保持诚实。

1361
01:11:41.620 --> 01:11:43.440
Like, Ben Patrick was doing sound.
比如，本·帕特里克（Ben Patrick）当时在负责收音。

1362
01:11:43.440 --> 01:11:47.000
And, you know, at one point he came to me, he was like, this isn't right.
有一次他走到我面前说，这不对劲。

1363
01:11:47.260 --> 01:11:48.920
You know, you're not doing it right.
你知道的，你做得不对。

1364
01:11:51.340 --> 01:11:54.120
And, you know, I had to talk him out of a tree at one point.
有一次我甚至得把他从树上劝下来。

1365
01:11:55.480 --> 01:11:55.840
But.
但是。

1366
01:11:56.260 --> 01:12:01.160
Well, one of the things that happened on the set when we were there, I think I can tell
嗯，我们在片场时发生过一件事，我想我可以讲

1367
01:12:01.160 --> 01:12:01.600
this story.
这个故事。

1368
01:12:01.740 --> 01:12:02.700
You tell me if not.
如果不行你告诉我。

1369
01:12:02.920 --> 01:12:05.060
But, and there was a section of people.
当时有一群人坐在那儿。

1370
01:12:05.300 --> 01:12:07.540
And so I thought, oh, I'll be friendly.
我想，哦，我要表现得友好一点。

1371
01:12:07.540 --> 01:12:11.280
And I'll just come over and I'll say, I'm like, oh, what do you all do on the show?
我就走过去说，哎，你们在剧里是做什么的？

1372
01:12:11.820 --> 01:12:14.240
And they all said, oh, we're employees.
他们都说，哦，我们是员工。

1373
01:12:14.480 --> 01:12:15.000
Oh, right.
哦，原来如此。

1374
01:12:15.160 --> 01:12:16.000
In the background.
在背景里。

1375
01:12:16.320 --> 01:12:16.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1376
01:12:16.780 --> 01:12:18.920
And we sit here all the time.
我们一直坐在这儿。

1377
01:12:19.180 --> 01:12:20.640
And that was their spot.
那是他们的位置。

1378
01:12:20.860 --> 01:12:22.080
And I was like, I did that.
我就说，我也做过那样的事。

1379
01:12:22.340 --> 01:12:23.600
I sat there.
我也坐在那儿。

1380
01:12:23.600 --> 01:12:25.220
We are on the show.
我们也在剧里。

1381
01:12:25.220 --> 01:12:28.940
But we're sitting here because we're in the background of this moment.
但我们坐在这儿是因为我们是这一幕的背景人物。

1382
01:12:29.200 --> 01:12:29.720
They're on deck.
他们正准备上场。

1383
01:12:30.020 --> 01:12:30.340
Yes.
是的。

1384
01:12:30.440 --> 01:12:33.520
And I was like, oh, my gosh, that's what we did.
我就想，天哪，那就是我们以前做的事。

1385
01:12:33.760 --> 01:12:35.660
We all sat there all the time.
我们以前总是坐在那儿。

1386
01:12:35.660 --> 01:12:42.980
And I think one of the reasons why our show was successful was because we were all there
我认为我们的剧之所以成功，原因之一就是我们大家都

1387
01:12:42.980 --> 01:12:43.740
all the time.
一直待在那里。

1388
01:12:43.920 --> 01:12:46.360
We were all in it all the time.
我们一直都全身心投入其中。

1389
01:12:46.640 --> 01:12:46.840
Yeah.
没错。

1390
01:12:47.100 --> 01:12:52.520
Well, there's a lot of reasons, I think, why our show worked.
嗯，我认为我们的剧之所以成功有很多原因。

1391
01:12:52.520 --> 01:12:55.060
I mean, the cast, first and foremoSt.
我是说，首先是演员阵容。

1392
01:12:55.060 --> 01:13:02.080
But the spirit of the cast and crew being in it together was very special.
但演员和剧组人员齐心协力的精神非常特别。

1393
01:13:02.440 --> 01:13:11.060
And I think I had a lot of theories about that I got from Monty Python, I think, which
我想我有很多关于这方面的理论是从《蒙提·派森》（Monty Python）那里学来的，我认为

1394
01:13:11.060 --> 01:13:12.600
was a huge show for me.
那对我来说是一部非常重要的剧。

1395
01:13:12.820 --> 01:13:16.600
Like when I'm 12, Monty Python comes out in the U.S.
比如我12岁时，《蒙提·派森》在美国上映。

1396
01:13:16.620 --> 01:13:21.660
And I'm just like, you know, when you're a 12-year-old, that's the comedy.
我就觉得，你知道，当你12岁时，那就是喜剧的巅峰。

1397
01:13:21.720 --> 01:13:23.020
I fought in your general direction.
我朝着你的方向战斗。

1398
01:13:23.020 --> 01:13:24.400
Yeah, no, exactly.
没错，完全正确。

1399
01:13:25.080 --> 01:13:26.580
Yeah, so we would always do that.
是啊，我们总是会那样做。

1400
01:13:26.740 --> 01:13:30.040
But I mean, the thing about Monty Python was the writers and the performers were the same
但我的意思是，《蒙提·派森》的特别之处在于编剧和表演者是同一批人。

1401
01:13:30.040 --> 01:13:30.460
people.
人们。

1402
01:13:31.040 --> 01:13:35.920
And you could just get this feeling of them all living in a house somewhere, getting weirder
你会有一种感觉，他们所有人都在某个地方住在一起，变得越来越古怪，

1403
01:13:35.920 --> 01:13:40.960
and weirder together, like this little, you know, cult that had split off from society.
一起变得越来越古怪，就像一个从社会中分裂出来的小型邪教组织。

1404
01:13:41.280 --> 01:13:45.220
Yeah, so I was definitely trying to encourage that with our little group.
没错，所以我绝对是在我们这个小团体里鼓励这种氛围。

1405
01:13:45.580 --> 01:13:51.280
Well, one of the things I love when I look back at pictures is that picture when we wrapped,
嗯，回顾照片时我最喜欢的一点，就是我们杀青时的那张照片，

1406
01:13:51.280 --> 01:13:58.040
you know, that final moment and how we were all in the scene together just walking out
你知道，那是最后时刻，我们所有人都在那个场景里，一起走出

1407
01:13:58.040 --> 01:14:06.300
of the building and the crew had all gathered around when you were about to yell, you know,
那栋建筑，而剧组人员都聚集在周围，当你准备喊出，你知道，

1408
01:14:06.560 --> 01:14:07.880
cut for the last time.
最后一次“卡”的时候。

1409
01:14:07.880 --> 01:14:13.180
I felt like that was our show, was that big room of people, you know.
我觉得那才是我们的剧，就是那一屋子人，你知道。

1410
01:14:13.380 --> 01:14:15.860
And we were missing our wrap party.
而且我们错过了杀青派对。

1411
01:14:16.000 --> 01:14:16.640
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

1412
01:14:16.760 --> 01:14:17.380
Yes, yes.
记得，记得。

1413
01:14:17.800 --> 01:14:18.280
Yes.
记得。

1414
01:14:18.420 --> 01:14:22.560
We were late to our own party, which is kind of perfect in itself.
我们自己的派对迟到了，这本身就挺完美的。

1415
01:14:22.700 --> 01:14:24.700
Yeah, because the party was doing the show.
是啊，因为派对就是拍戏的过程。

1416
01:14:24.880 --> 01:14:26.600
So nobody wanted that party to end.
所以没人想让那个派对结束。

1417
01:14:26.820 --> 01:14:27.120
No.
没错。

1418
01:14:27.220 --> 01:14:32.180
And the party where you're drinking ginger ale in some rented warehouse was not going to be
而那个在某个租来的仓库里喝姜汁汽水的派对，肯定不会

1419
01:14:32.180 --> 01:14:32.580
as good.
那么棒。

1420
01:14:32.580 --> 01:14:34.280
As right that moment.
比不上那一刻。

1421
01:14:34.400 --> 01:14:34.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1422
01:14:35.420 --> 01:14:38.240
That's one of the moments I would do again, I think.
我想那是我想重温的时刻之一。

1423
01:14:38.660 --> 01:14:40.480
You would wrap the series again?
你想重温一遍剧集杀青吗？

1424
01:14:40.700 --> 01:14:41.720
No, just that.
不，就那一刻。

1425
01:14:41.840 --> 01:14:44.320
But that's what I mean, like that moment of camaraderie.
但我就是那个意思，那种情谊的时刻。

1426
01:14:44.320 --> 01:14:46.700
That feeling of camaraderie is really special.
那种情谊的感觉真的很特别。

1427
01:14:46.700 --> 01:14:49.040
And there's that amazing picture.
还有那张很棒的照片。

1428
01:14:49.040 --> 01:14:56.700
And I don't know why I'm tearing up, but I think just because it's that moment when we
我不知道为什么我会热泪盈眶，但我认为只是因为那一刻我们

1429
01:14:56.700 --> 01:15:04.440
sort of collectively said goodbye was so powerful and just special.
集体告别的方式太震撼、太特别了。

1430
01:15:04.760 --> 01:15:05.480
And, you know.
而且，你知道。

1431
01:15:05.640 --> 01:15:07.420
The finale really turned out well.
大结局确实拍得很好。

1432
01:15:07.880 --> 01:15:08.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1433
01:15:08.560 --> 01:15:08.880
Didn't it?
不是吗？

1434
01:15:08.980 --> 01:15:09.080
It did.
确实。

1435
01:15:09.080 --> 01:15:09.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1436
01:15:09.540 --> 01:15:14.240
I think that makes a big difference because I think there's so many people who watch the
我认为这有很大的不同，因为我觉得有很多人看完

1437
01:15:14.240 --> 01:15:19.680
finale and then they just crank it up to season one again and start watching again.
大结局后，又会直接调回第一季重新开始看。

1438
01:15:20.100 --> 01:15:20.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1439
01:15:20.660 --> 01:15:21.600
I get it.
我明白。

1440
01:15:21.840 --> 01:15:22.520
I really get it.
我真的明白。

1441
01:15:22.620 --> 01:15:27.940
In our rewatch and having seen some of these episodes I haven't seen since we made them,
在我们重温的过程中，看到了一些自拍摄以来我就没再看过的剧集，

1442
01:15:28.440 --> 01:15:30.660
I'm just like, I'm ready to start again.
我就觉得，我已经准备好重新开始了。

1443
01:15:30.920 --> 01:15:34.560
Like we watched the pilot yesterday and I'm like, well, I'm ready to watch it again.
就像我们昨天看了试播集，我就觉得，好吧，我已经准备好再看一遍了。

1444
01:15:34.820 --> 01:15:35.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1445
01:15:35.180 --> 01:15:36.280
We change.
我们变了。

1446
01:15:36.520 --> 01:15:43.580
The characters do grow, but they grow really slowly in a way that's very satisfying.
角色确实在成长，但他们的成长非常缓慢，以一种非常令人满意的方式。

1447
01:15:43.700 --> 01:15:49.520
And so I think that's one of the things that is enjoyable about watching it again and again
所以我认为这就是一遍又一遍地观看

1448
01:15:49.520 --> 01:15:54.620
and starting over is that you really are starting at the beginning of a journey with these people.
并重新开始的乐趣所在，因为你确实是在和这些人一起开启一段旅程的起点。

1449
01:15:54.740 --> 01:15:58.800
And it's kind of even fun to know now where they're going to end up.
而且现在知道他们的结局如何，甚至更有趣了。

1450
01:15:58.800 --> 01:15:58.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1451
01:15:59.120 --> 01:15:59.740
Yeah, for sure.
没错，确实如此。

1452
01:15:59.900 --> 01:16:01.900
As you go back and watch the second time.
当你回头看第二遍的时候。

1453
01:16:01.900 --> 01:16:08.100
Have you ever seen a documentary that was called 7 Up when it started?
你看过一部叫《7 Up》的纪录片吗？从它刚开始的时候。

1454
01:16:08.240 --> 01:16:08.480
Yes.
看过。

1455
01:16:08.740 --> 01:16:10.560
14 Up, 21 Up.
《14 Up》、《21 Up》。

1456
01:16:10.920 --> 01:16:12.420
I don't know what they're up to now.
我不知道他们现在拍到多少岁了。

1457
01:16:12.520 --> 01:16:14.000
They're like 63 Up or something.
好像是《63 Up》之类的吧。

1458
01:16:14.260 --> 01:16:21.060
But it's every seven years they check in with this group of British people who start as seven-year-olds.
但它是每七年回访一次这群英国人，从他们七岁时就开始了。

1459
01:16:21.740 --> 01:16:22.300
Yeah.
是的。

1460
01:16:22.460 --> 01:16:25.860
It's really moving to see what happens to them.
看着他们的经历真的让人很感动。

1461
01:16:26.580 --> 01:16:34.780
But I think that part of the bones of the show is that it is a documentary for real,
但我认为这部剧的精髓在于它是一部真实的纪录片，

1462
01:16:34.780 --> 01:16:41.040
and it can tap into some of the things that make documentaries emotional.
它能触及一些让纪录片变得感人的特质。

1463
01:16:41.560 --> 01:16:43.680
And the finale was like that.
大结局也是这样。

1464
01:16:43.820 --> 01:16:48.640
It was kind of like people summing their lives up and, you know.
就像人们在总结自己的人生一样，你懂的。

1465
01:16:48.640 --> 01:16:49.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

1466
01:16:49.340 --> 01:16:49.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1467
01:16:49.800 --> 01:16:50.060
Yeah.
没错。

1468
01:16:50.400 --> 01:16:58.740
Because when you go back and watch the pilot in this superfan version that we watched was a Jim talking head that was extended that I hadn't seen.
因为当你回头看我们看的那个“超级粉丝版”试播集时，里面有一段吉姆的访谈，那是加长版的，我之前没看过。

1469
01:16:58.980 --> 01:16:59.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

1470
01:16:59.640 --> 01:17:02.160
And that's one of the things in the rewatch.
这也是重温这部剧的乐趣之一。

1471
01:17:02.300 --> 01:17:07.800
There's so many talking heads I hadn't seen because we're not there when we film each other's talking heads, you know.
有太多我没看过的访谈片段了，因为我们拍各自的访谈时并不在场，你知道的。

1472
01:17:08.020 --> 01:17:08.140
Right, right.
对，没错。

1473
01:17:08.140 --> 01:17:09.980
So there's all these kind of surprises.
所以会有各种各样的惊喜。

1474
01:17:10.400 --> 01:17:14.300
And Jim says, well, let's see.
吉姆说，嗯，让我想想。

1475
01:17:14.520 --> 01:17:15.500
I'm not married.
我没结婚。

1476
01:17:15.500 --> 01:17:16.680
I don't have kids.
我没有孩子。

1477
01:17:17.200 --> 01:17:19.140
But I was able to buy a car.
但我买得起一辆车。

1478
01:17:19.280 --> 01:17:20.760
So I have a car.
所以我有一辆车。

1479
01:17:21.160 --> 01:17:23.860
And my car is five years old.
我的车已经开了五年了。

1480
01:17:24.880 --> 01:17:33.860
And I'm just like – then I think about like all the places that – where Jim goes, you know, and where he ends up and his life.
我当时就在想——然后我想到吉姆去过的地方，他最终的归宿和他的人生。

1481
01:17:33.860 --> 01:17:37.980
And I was just thinking about that, that that's exactly what you're talking about.
我刚才就在想这个，这正是你所说的。

1482
01:17:38.080 --> 01:17:42.820
I felt like I had watched him become his fully realized self.
我觉得我看着他成为了一个完整的人。

1483
01:17:43.320 --> 01:17:48.800
A lot of the extras for the pilot were stuff that I had added to the British script.
试播集里的很多额外内容都是我从英版剧本里加进去的。

1484
01:17:48.980 --> 01:17:58.700
And then when we had to cut it down to time, a lot of those had to go because the original story had all the beats in it.
后来为了缩减时长，很多内容不得不删掉，因为原版故事已经包含了所有的剧情节点。

1485
01:17:58.780 --> 01:18:01.920
But a lot of those little grace notes were nice.
但那些小小的点缀真的很棒。

1486
01:18:01.920 --> 01:18:05.680
Well, the super fan episode is really satisfying to watch.
嗯，超级粉丝版剧集看起来真的很过瘾。

1487
01:18:05.800 --> 01:18:07.420
It's really, really fun to watch.
看的时候真的非常非常开心。

1488
01:18:07.540 --> 01:18:08.180
Oh, that's good.
哦，那太好了。

1489
01:18:08.340 --> 01:18:18.560
And you get to feel that difference between the British pilot and then where you can know that our show is eventually going.
你能感受到英版试播集与我们剧集最终走向之间的差异。

1490
01:18:18.560 --> 01:18:19.360
Is aiming at it.
也就是我们的目标所在。

1491
01:18:19.440 --> 01:18:19.880
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，没错。

1492
01:18:20.020 --> 01:18:20.340
It's cool.
这很酷。

1493
01:18:20.480 --> 01:18:23.460
I like that we've watched the whole original broadcaSt.
我很高兴我们看完了最初播出的所有内容。

1494
01:18:23.520 --> 01:18:28.260
And now we get to see – it's like we got a dessert, you know.
现在我们又能看到这些——就像吃到了甜点一样，你懂的。

1495
01:18:28.340 --> 01:18:28.600
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1496
01:18:28.600 --> 01:18:29.840
And I appreciate it.
我很感激。

1497
01:18:29.840 --> 01:18:30.720
And then, you know,
而且你知道，

1498
01:18:30.800 --> 01:18:43.480
we were talking to Dave Rogers about it and just the absolute care and integrity that he wants to make sure that these super fan episodes do not venture too far off the original mission.
我们和戴夫·罗杰斯聊过这件事，他那种绝对的严谨和诚意，确保这些超级粉丝版剧集不会偏离最初的创作初衷。

1499
01:18:43.740 --> 01:18:46.460
And I'm just like they could not be in better hands.
我当时就觉得，交给他就再放心不过了。

1500
01:18:46.640 --> 01:18:48.840
And I know he's working directly with you on them.
而且我知道他正在和你直接合作制作这些内容。

1501
01:18:48.840 --> 01:18:54.060
And we're so thankful that Dave is sort of helping with all of that.
我们非常感谢戴夫在这些方面提供的帮助。

1502
01:18:54.240 --> 01:18:55.000
Oh, God, yeah.
天哪，确实。

1503
01:18:55.340 --> 01:18:59.300
Well, Dave is really the custodian of every moment of the show.
嗯，戴夫确实是这部剧每一个瞬间的守护者。

1504
01:18:59.600 --> 01:19:01.620
Oh, that's such a beautiful phrase.
哦，这个说法真美。

1505
01:19:01.920 --> 01:19:02.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1506
01:19:02.300 --> 01:19:02.460
Yeah.
没错。

1507
01:19:02.500 --> 01:19:04.360
He just knows everything about it.
他对这部剧的一切了如指掌。

1508
01:19:04.560 --> 01:19:04.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1509
01:19:05.160 --> 01:19:08.560
As opposed to me who's like Mrs. 6.0 joke.
不像我，我简直就是个“六分笑话”女士。

1510
01:19:09.880 --> 01:19:10.880
And Joe Bennett.
还有乔·贝内特。

1511
01:19:11.960 --> 01:19:18.320
Well, before we move on to the final part of this interview, I know everybody's going to want us to ask.
那么，在进入采访的最后一部分之前，我知道大家肯定希望我们问这个问题。

1512
01:19:18.320 --> 01:19:20.360
You don't have to answer.
你可以不回答。

1513
01:19:20.840 --> 01:19:27.520
But we have to ask you about this news story that came out about a certain somebody who might be on the paper.
但我们必须问问你关于那篇新闻报道的事，关于某个可能出现在报纸上的人。

1514
01:19:28.180 --> 01:19:28.660
Yes.
是的。

1515
01:19:28.820 --> 01:19:32.520
A certain character from the office, Oscar.
《办公室》里的某个角色，奥斯卡。

1516
01:19:33.140 --> 01:19:33.420
Yes.
是的。

1517
01:19:33.520 --> 01:19:34.660
Well, we can now confirm.
好吧，我们现在可以确认了。

1518
01:19:34.660 --> 01:19:39.900
You remember that when you visited the set, it was extreme secrecy.
你还记得你探班的时候，那是极度保密的。

1519
01:19:40.060 --> 01:19:41.880
Yes, he wasn't even called Oscar.
是的，他甚至不叫奥斯卡。

1520
01:19:42.140 --> 01:19:42.380
No.
没错。

1521
01:19:42.380 --> 01:19:43.800
Like on the script and stuff.
比如在剧本之类的东西上。

1522
01:19:44.260 --> 01:19:51.360
Well, my hope was that the first promo or the first piece of footage that it would be a surprise to the audience.
嗯，我原本希望第一个宣传片或第一段片段能给观众一个惊喜。

1523
01:19:51.360 --> 01:19:53.480
Like when Steve showed up in the finale?
就像史蒂夫在大结局中出现那样？

1524
01:19:53.480 --> 01:19:54.000
Yes.
是的。

1525
01:19:54.000 --> 01:19:59.240
It's very difficult to keep a surprise nowadays with the amount of entertainment journalism.
如今在娱乐新闻如此发达的情况下，想要保持惊喜感非常困难。

1526
01:19:59.660 --> 01:20:00.880
And somebody sniffed it out.
结果还是有人嗅到了风声。

1527
01:20:01.120 --> 01:20:01.220
How?
怎么会？

1528
01:20:02.520 --> 01:20:04.300
How did someone sniff it out?
怎么会有人嗅到风声的？

1529
01:20:04.380 --> 01:20:05.000
I don't know.
我不知道。

1530
01:20:05.200 --> 01:20:16.780
But, you know, I mean, there was a lot of times where the tram would go by and Oscar would like dive behind a trash can or something.
但是，你知道，有很多次电车经过时，奥斯卡都会躲到垃圾桶后面之类的。

1531
01:20:16.960 --> 01:20:25.860
When we were visiting, the tram went by and the NBC, the coordinator who had coordinated our visit, they were like, move away, move away from the tram.
我们去探班时，电车经过，负责协调我们行程的NBC工作人员就说，快走开，离电车远点。

1532
01:20:26.160 --> 01:20:28.580
Like they didn't want the tram to see us visiting.
就好像他们不想让电车上的人看到我们在探班一样。

1533
01:20:28.580 --> 01:20:30.020
And we dove behind a trailer.
于是我们躲到了拖车后面。

1534
01:20:30.600 --> 01:20:37.860
And then a woman who just happened to be walking through the lot saw us and was like, oh, my gosh, and asked for our picture.
然后一个刚好路过片场的女士看到了我们，惊呼道“天哪”，并要求和我们合影。

1535
01:20:38.100 --> 01:20:39.000
And we said yes.
我们答应了。

1536
01:20:39.000 --> 01:20:39.720
We're like, sure.
我们当时想，当然可以。

1537
01:20:40.000 --> 01:20:43.720
And that NBC woman sprinted out and said, you have to, you can't post that.
结果那个NBC的工作人员冲过来，说你们必须，你们不能发那张照片。

1538
01:20:43.720 --> 01:20:44.400
You can't.
绝对不行。

1539
01:20:44.400 --> 01:20:45.460
And we were like, oh.
我们当时就想，哦。

1540
01:20:45.760 --> 01:20:47.480
And she was like, okay, you guys get in your cars.
然后她说，好吧，你们快上车。

1541
01:20:47.760 --> 01:20:48.380
Like, yeah.
就是这样。

1542
01:20:48.380 --> 01:20:57.180
Well, it's interesting because I always feel like it's more fun for surprises to hit while you're having the experience of watching the show.
嗯，这很有趣，因为我总觉得惊喜在观看节目的过程中出现会更有意思。

1543
01:20:57.180 --> 01:21:11.580
And for an ordinary person who is going to watch the show several years later without paying attention to whatever the pre-launch publicity was, blogs and stuff,
对于一个几年后才看这部剧，且没关注任何发布前宣传、博客之类的普通观众来说，

1544
01:21:11.880 --> 01:21:13.040
is just going to be watching it.
他们只是在看剧而已。

1545
01:21:13.140 --> 01:21:18.100
So you want to build it so that the surprises are for the people watching the show.
所以你希望在制作时，这些惊喜是留给看剧的人的。

1546
01:21:19.240 --> 01:21:24.620
But sometimes it's very difficult to promote things if you're going to try and keep a secret.
但有时候，如果你想保守秘密，宣传工作会变得非常困难。

1547
01:21:24.980 --> 01:21:32.480
And so, for instance, I am also putting the finishing touches on the last season of Upload, season four.
比如，我目前也在为《上载新生》的最后一季，也就是第四季做收尾工作。

1548
01:21:32.480 --> 01:21:43.020
And we ended season three on an enormous cliffhanger of which version of our lead character, Nathan, Robbie Amell.
我们在第三季结尾留下了一个巨大的悬念，关于我们主角内森（罗比·阿梅尔饰）的哪个版本。

1549
01:21:43.240 --> 01:21:46.500
He's, you know, a digital person who's been uploaded.
他，你知道，是一个被上传的数字人。

1550
01:21:46.720 --> 01:21:53.060
And at some point he was illegally copied and there's two of them in season three.
在某个节点他被非法复制了，所以在第三季里有两个他。

1551
01:21:53.060 --> 01:21:57.080
And then we sort of ended on this cliffhanger of one of them has been destroyed.
然后我们以其中一个被摧毁的悬念结束了上一季。

1552
01:21:57.080 --> 01:22:00.300
And anyway, so we were like, oh, cool.
总之，当时我们觉得，哦，挺酷的。

1553
01:22:00.440 --> 01:22:04.480
It's going to be such an exciting beginning to season four when you find out which one.
当第四季开播，大家发现究竟是哪一个被摧毁时，那将会是一个非常令人兴奋的开端。

1554
01:22:04.620 --> 01:22:11.280
And now I'm realizing, like, I don't know how to promote this because all of the, you know, any clip.
现在我才意识到，我不知道该怎么宣传这一季，因为所有的，你知道，任何片段。

1555
01:22:11.380 --> 01:22:12.720
All of the footage is very clear.
所有的镜头都非常清晰。

1556
01:22:12.760 --> 01:22:15.860
It's going to make it pretty clear which one, you know, which one survived.
这会让人很清楚地看出，你知道，究竟是哪一个幸存了下来。

1557
01:22:16.040 --> 01:22:18.280
But I wasn't thinking along those lines.
但我当时没往那方面想。

1558
01:22:19.360 --> 01:22:31.020
But, yeah, so I was really trying to protect Oscar to be a fun surprise for people watching the new show to suddenly realize that he was a part of it.
不过，是的，我当时真的很想保护奥斯卡这个惊喜，让看新剧的人突然发现他也是其中的一部分。

1559
01:22:31.200 --> 01:22:37.440
And, you know, and the essential story of the show, I mean, Oscar is wonderful.
而且，你知道，这部剧的核心故事，我是说，奥斯卡很棒。

1560
01:22:37.500 --> 01:22:40.760
It's not the spinoff series for what happens to Oscar.
这不是一部关于奥斯卡后续发展的衍生剧。

1561
01:22:40.760 --> 01:23:00.400
It's more the show of the documentary crew looking around for something else to do a documentary about and finding this newspaper that has fallen on hard times like most newspapers and does not even have a budget for any reporters.
这部剧更多是关于纪录片摄制组在寻找其他拍摄题材时，发现了这家陷入困境的报社，就像大多数报社一样，甚至连雇佣记者的预算都没有。

1562
01:23:00.400 --> 01:23:12.840
So the idea is that a very, you know, idealistic person comes in to try and put this newspaper back on his feet and finds out that's Donald Gleason,
所以构思是一个非常有理想的人进来试图让这家报社重振旗鼓，他发现那是唐纳德·格里森，

1563
01:23:13.080 --> 01:23:22.780
finds out that he doesn't have the budget to hire reporters and has to turn the existing staff of ad salespeople and, you know,
他发现自己没有预算去雇佣记者，不得不把现有的广告销售人员，你知道，

1564
01:23:22.980 --> 01:23:29.100
accountants and truck drivers into reporters to make some content for the paper.
会计和卡车司机变成记者，为报纸制作内容。

1565
01:23:29.100 --> 01:23:33.280
And they don't know what they're doing and, you know, hilarity ensues.
他们根本不知道自己在做什么，然后，你知道，笑料百出。

1566
01:23:35.440 --> 01:23:37.500
Well, we're so excited to watch it.
太好了，我们非常期待观看。

1567
01:23:37.660 --> 01:23:39.520
Do you know when it's going to air?
你知道它什么时候播出吗？

1568
01:23:39.840 --> 01:23:41.040
Do you have an air date?
有具体的播出日期吗？

1569
01:23:42.440 --> 01:23:48.340
I think probably in the fall, like a back to school kind of a thing.
我想大概是在秋季，就像开学季那种感觉。

1570
01:23:48.360 --> 01:23:48.540
Okay.
好的。

1571
01:23:48.740 --> 01:23:50.360
Like it's like the old days.
就像过去的老日子一样。

1572
01:23:50.580 --> 01:23:54.620
Well, we can't wait to watch the paper and you'll let us know when we can start sharing about it.
好吧，我们迫不及待想看这部剧了，到时候请告诉我们什么时候可以开始分享相关内容。

1573
01:23:54.820 --> 01:23:55.120
Yes.
好的。

1574
01:23:55.600 --> 01:23:56.000
Of course.
当然。

1575
01:23:56.200 --> 01:23:56.320
Yes.
好的。

1576
01:23:56.480 --> 01:23:56.680
Okay.
好的。

1577
01:23:56.860 --> 01:23:57.160
Thank you.
谢谢。

1578
01:23:57.160 --> 01:24:00.440
So, Greg, we've started asking our guests the call sheet questions.
那么，格雷格，我们开始问嘉宾“通告单问题”了。

1579
01:24:00.580 --> 01:24:01.380
That's what we call them.
我们是这么叫它们的。

1580
01:24:01.660 --> 01:24:05.340
These were the questions on the back of our call sheets where we would get to know a crew member.
这些问题曾印在我们通告单的背面，用来了解剧组人员。

1581
01:24:05.580 --> 01:24:09.220
So we're going to ask you the office call sheet questions.
所以我们要问你《办公室》的通告单问题。

1582
01:24:09.420 --> 01:24:09.740
Okay.
好的。

1583
01:24:10.300 --> 01:24:10.620
Ready?
准备好了吗？

1584
01:24:10.920 --> 01:24:12.240
Question number one.
第一个问题。

1585
01:24:12.900 --> 01:24:15.260
What was your first entertainment job?
你的第一份娱乐行业工作是什么？

1586
01:24:16.040 --> 01:24:16.800
Ah-ha-ha.
啊哈哈。

1587
01:24:18.960 --> 01:24:33.740
Well, I'll tell you that I track it from, it's not really a job, but my father worked for Capital Cities Broadcasting as his career when I was a kid.
嗯，我得告诉你，我追溯到——那不算真正的工作，但我小时候，我父亲在首都城市广播公司工作。

1588
01:24:33.740 --> 01:24:35.460
And he worked at different radio stations.
他在不同的广播电台工作过。

1589
01:24:35.900 --> 01:24:43.560
And at one point, he was the manager of a rock radio station in Rhode Island.
有一次，他是罗德岛一家摇滚电台的经理。

1590
01:24:43.560 --> 01:24:51.760
And he used to go to this manager's meeting for all of the other station managers.
他经常去参加其他电台经理的会议。

1591
01:24:52.090 --> 01:24:55.420
And he entertained at the meeting.
他在会议上表演节目。

1592
01:24:55.420 --> 01:25:10.800
He had a Karnak-style act where he would put an envelope up to his head and read the answers and then open up the envelope and there would be the joke.
他有一个卡纳克风格的表演，把信封贴在额头上读出答案，然后打开信封，里面就是笑话。

1593
01:25:10.800 --> 01:25:18.420
And so I wrote jokes for him for that act.
所以我为他的那个表演写过笑话。

1594
01:25:18.420 --> 01:25:20.460
And we've used it in the show.
我们在剧里也用过这个桥段。

1595
01:25:20.780 --> 01:25:21.400
I remember that.
我记得那个。

1596
01:25:21.400 --> 01:25:21.640
Do you remember this?
你还记得吗？

1597
01:25:21.940 --> 01:25:22.940
When Michael does it.
迈克尔做那个的时候。

1598
01:25:22.960 --> 01:25:23.240
Yes.
是的。

1599
01:25:23.320 --> 01:25:24.260
And we used the same joke.
我们用了同一个笑话。

1600
01:25:24.400 --> 01:25:25.380
That was my first joke.
那是我写的第一个笑话。

1601
01:25:26.000 --> 01:25:27.020
How old were you?
你当时多大？

1602
01:25:27.100 --> 01:25:28.060
I was like a teenager.
我大概十几岁吧。

1603
01:25:28.340 --> 01:25:30.180
And he did it for many years.
他做了很多年。

1604
01:25:30.180 --> 01:25:34.380
And eventually, various friends of mine wrote for him.
后来，我的一些朋友也为他写过稿子。

1605
01:25:34.380 --> 01:25:45.740
And at one point, he had Conan writing for him and this guy, Mike Reese, who was one of the showrunners of The Simpsons, who before – and obviously before, you know,
有段时间，柯南（Conan）和迈克·里斯（Mike Reese）都在为他写稿，迈克后来成了《辛普森一家》的剧集主管之一，当然是在那之前，你知道的，

1606
01:25:46.260 --> 01:25:48.740
they had big careers.
他们后来都事业有成。

1607
01:25:49.100 --> 01:25:57.400
So in your dad's, like, employee circle and just circle of friends, do they just think your dad is the funniest person they've ever met?
那么在你父亲的员工圈子和朋友圈里，他们是不是都觉得你父亲是他们见过最幽默的人？

1608
01:25:57.680 --> 01:26:00.620
He had, like, the best comedy writers writing for him.
他当时雇佣的都是最顶尖的喜剧编剧。

1609
01:26:00.620 --> 01:26:01.600
I've stolen a ton of stories.
我偷用了他不少故事。

1610
01:26:01.600 --> 01:26:06.660
My dad has, like, lived through a lot of funny things, and he turns them into very funny stories.
我父亲经历过很多有趣的事，他总能把这些事变成非常搞笑的故事。

1611
01:26:06.660 --> 01:26:08.080
And I've used them.
我也用过这些故事。

1612
01:26:08.200 --> 01:26:17.340
So, for instance, I wrote an episode of Seinfeld that was 100% based on my dad where, you know, he lived in New York City and he had a car,
比如，我写过一集《宋飞正传》，百分之百取材于我父亲，你知道，他当时住在纽约市，有一辆车，

1613
01:26:17.380 --> 01:26:19.280
but it was too expensive to have a garage.
但租车库太贵了。

1614
01:26:19.280 --> 01:26:23.640
So every two days he would drive around looking for a parking space.
所以每隔两天，他就得开车到处找停车位。

1615
01:26:23.800 --> 01:26:27.040
And sometimes it would take 45 minutes, an hour to find a parking space.
有时候得花上四十五分钟甚至一小时才能找到一个车位。

1616
01:26:27.040 --> 01:26:29.240
So at one point, he found one.
有一次，他终于找到了一个。

1617
01:26:29.240 --> 01:26:31.380
He was so excited, and he started to back into it.
他特别兴奋，开始倒车入位。

1618
01:26:31.520 --> 01:26:33.860
And this other guy tried to front into it.
结果另一个人想直接开进去。

1619
01:26:34.060 --> 01:26:35.640
And neither of them would budge.
两人谁也不肯让步。

1620
01:26:35.640 --> 01:26:35.820
I remember that episode.
我记得那一集。

1621
01:26:35.820 --> 01:26:36.380
Do you remember this episode?
你还记得那一集吗？

1622
01:26:36.620 --> 01:26:39.060
Yes, and it was like a standoff in the parking spot.
记得，就像是在停车位上的对峙一样。

1623
01:26:39.140 --> 01:26:39.340
Yeah.
没错。

1624
01:26:39.520 --> 01:26:42.620
And this happened to him, and he wouldn't leave.
这事儿真发生在他身上，他就是不肯走。

1625
01:26:42.700 --> 01:26:51.380
And a friend of his walked by, and he flagged him down, and he had him, you know, tell my mom to make him dinner and bring it to the parking spot.
正好有个朋友路过，他把人叫住，让人去告诉我妈，让她做顿晚饭送到停车位那儿来。

1626
01:26:54.060 --> 01:26:59.800
And, you know, so I pitched that to Larry David and, you know, sold that as a freelance episode.
然后，我就把这个点子提给了拉里·大卫（Larry David），并作为自由撰稿人卖掉了那一集。

1627
01:27:00.220 --> 01:27:09.300
So I feel like I've taken enough from him where I'm happy to have given him, you know, jokes for his manager act.
所以我感觉我从他那儿拿的够多了，能为他的经纪人表演写写笑话，我也很乐意。

1628
01:27:09.620 --> 01:27:10.560
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

1629
01:27:10.720 --> 01:27:11.460
I love that so much.
我太喜欢这个了。

1630
01:27:11.460 --> 01:27:11.980
So that would be my firSt.
那算是我的第一份工作吧。

1631
01:27:12.060 --> 01:27:13.340
I mean, that wasn't a paid job.
我是说，那不是一份带薪工作。

1632
01:27:13.340 --> 01:27:23.000
First paid job was Conan and I probably working for not necessarily the news back in the day.
第一份带薪工作是我和柯南一起做的，当时我们可能不是在给新闻节目写稿。

1633
01:27:23.200 --> 01:27:24.320
As writing partners?
是以写作搭档的身份吗？

1634
01:27:24.480 --> 01:27:25.540
Yes, we were writing partners.
是的，我们是写作搭档。

1635
01:27:25.860 --> 01:27:25.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1636
01:27:26.680 --> 01:27:27.680
Next question.
下一个问题。

1637
01:27:27.920 --> 01:27:31.820
Do you speak any other languages or play a musical instrument?
你会说其他语言或者演奏乐器吗？

1638
01:27:32.240 --> 01:27:37.100
It's so funny you should bring that up because I am pounding away at Duolingo right now.
你提到这个太有意思了，因为我最近正在死磕多邻国（Duolingo）。

1639
01:27:37.260 --> 01:27:37.800
What language?
什么语言？

1640
01:27:37.800 --> 01:27:45.060
I'm doing Spanish and French and Portuguese and, like, Japanese.
我在学西班牙语、法语、葡萄牙语，还有日语什么的。

1641
01:27:45.300 --> 01:27:46.220
I'm trying a whole bunch.
我试了很多种。

1642
01:27:46.420 --> 01:27:47.860
To see what sticks?
看看哪种能学进去？

1643
01:27:48.280 --> 01:27:48.640
Yeah.
对。

1644
01:27:48.760 --> 01:27:51.020
Well, sometimes you're, you know, mostly Spanish.
嗯，有时候你，你知道，主要是西班牙语。

1645
01:27:51.380 --> 01:27:55.560
I'm making the most progress in Spanish, but sometimes I'll try some other ones.
我在西班牙语上进展最快，但偶尔也会尝试其他的。

1646
01:27:55.560 --> 01:28:06.660
And I just was at McCabe's Guitar Shop last week and I was listening to a concert and somebody was playing a mandolin.
上周我刚去了麦凯布吉他店（McCabe's Guitar Shop），听了一场音乐会，有人在弹曼陀林琴。

1647
01:28:06.840 --> 01:28:07.860
And I was like, God damn it.
当时我就想，该死。

1648
01:28:07.880 --> 01:28:10.200
I got to learn how to play the mandolin before I die.
我一定要在死之前学会弹曼陀林。

1649
01:28:10.480 --> 01:28:12.740
I really want to learn that.
我真的很想学那个。

1650
01:28:12.840 --> 01:28:14.980
But I have really no musical ability.
但我确实没什么音乐天赋。

1651
01:28:15.260 --> 01:28:16.880
So Creed plays the mandolin.
所以克里德会弹曼陀林。

1652
01:28:16.980 --> 01:28:17.240
Does he?
真的吗？

1653
01:28:17.380 --> 01:28:18.440
I'll bet he's great.
我敢说他一定很厉害。

1654
01:28:18.980 --> 01:28:19.640
All right.
好吧。

1655
01:28:19.760 --> 01:28:20.620
Next question.
下一个问题。

1656
01:28:21.100 --> 01:28:24.340
What's a place you've been to that you absolutely loved?
你去过什么地方是你绝对喜欢的？

1657
01:28:24.340 --> 01:28:30.740
Well, I'm, like, kind of, like, no matter where I go, I'm always like, could I live here?
嗯，我，怎么说呢，不管我去哪儿，我总是会想，我能住在这儿吗？

1658
01:28:31.060 --> 01:28:31.940
This is cool.
这感觉很棒。

1659
01:28:32.300 --> 01:28:36.160
And I remember driving out to L.A.
我记得当时开车去洛杉矶。

1660
01:28:36.820 --> 01:28:43.700
with Conan and another friend, Rob Lezevnik, to have jobs at not necessarily the news.
和柯南还有另一个朋友罗伯·莱泽夫尼克一起，去那儿找工作，不一定是去新闻界。

1661
01:28:43.700 --> 01:28:45.540
And we drove through Santa Fe, New Mexico.
我们开车经过了新墨西哥州的圣达菲。

1662
01:28:46.020 --> 01:28:49.420
And I remember being like, oh, my God, this place is magical.
我记得当时我就想，天哪，这地方太神奇了。

1663
01:28:49.680 --> 01:28:50.680
How could I work here?
我怎么才能在这儿工作呢？

1664
01:28:50.680 --> 01:28:58.800
And the only job that I thought I might be able to work on was the newspaper because they had a newspaper there.
我唯一能想到能做的工作就是报社，因为他们那儿有报纸。

1665
01:28:59.000 --> 01:29:05.440
So I had a little fantasy of living in Santa Fe and working for whatever their newspaper was.
所以我当时幻想过住在圣达菲，为他们的报社工作。

1666
01:29:05.640 --> 01:29:07.540
My in-laws live in Santa Fe.
我的岳父母住在圣达菲。

1667
01:29:07.640 --> 01:29:07.880
Really?
真的吗？

1668
01:29:08.060 --> 01:29:08.240
Yeah.
是的。

1669
01:29:08.380 --> 01:29:10.920
Lee's dad and stepmom live in Santa Fe.
李的父亲和继母住在圣达菲。

1670
01:29:11.080 --> 01:29:11.660
We go there all the time.
我们经常去那儿。

1671
01:29:11.660 --> 01:29:12.760
I love the smell of the air there.
我喜欢那儿空气的味道。

1672
01:29:13.500 --> 01:29:17.680
Well, you know, it's very high elevation, actually.
嗯，你知道，那儿海拔其实很高。

1673
01:29:18.060 --> 01:29:19.220
Kind of sneaks up on you.
会让你有点措手不及。

1674
01:29:19.340 --> 01:29:25.340
But we moved to Santa Fe during the pandemic to be closer to them, and that was our pod.
但我们在疫情期间搬到了圣达菲，为了离他们近一点，那是我们的防疫小圈子。

1675
01:29:25.980 --> 01:29:26.680
That's cool.
那很酷。

1676
01:29:27.040 --> 01:29:28.380
I mean, that's really cool.
我是说，那真的很酷。

1677
01:29:28.380 --> 01:29:28.840
It's great.
那太棒了。

1678
01:29:29.100 --> 01:29:29.600
It's great.
那太棒了。

1679
01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:30.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1680
01:29:30.680 --> 01:29:30.920
Okay.
好的。

1681
01:29:31.460 --> 01:29:32.540
Question number four.
第四个问题。

1682
01:29:32.540 --> 01:29:34.200
What do you like to do on the weekends?
你周末喜欢做什么？

1683
01:29:35.120 --> 01:29:40.320
Well, you know, I still have kids who can't drive.
嗯，你知道，我还有孩子不会开车。

1684
01:29:40.700 --> 01:29:42.940
My youngest is just learning how to drive.
我最小的孩子刚开始学开车。

1685
01:29:43.380 --> 01:29:48.660
And so my weekends are mostly driving her around.
所以我的周末大部分时间都在开车接送她。

1686
01:29:49.140 --> 01:29:49.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1687
01:29:49.780 --> 01:29:50.500
I can relate.
我深有同感。

1688
01:29:50.840 --> 01:29:51.460
I say something.
我说点什么。

1689
01:29:51.560 --> 01:29:53.260
I'm just parent Uber, you know?
我就是个家长版优步司机，你懂的。

1690
01:29:53.980 --> 01:29:54.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1691
01:29:54.480 --> 01:29:54.820
So.
所以。

1692
01:29:55.520 --> 01:29:57.400
That's what you do on the weekends.
这就是你周末做的事。

1693
01:29:57.760 --> 01:29:58.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1694
01:29:58.140 --> 01:29:59.940
What do you like to do on the weekends?
那你周末喜欢做什么？

1695
01:30:00.060 --> 01:30:00.760
I don't need to.
我不需要做什么。

1696
01:30:00.960 --> 01:30:01.440
There's no.
没必要。

1697
01:30:01.440 --> 01:30:07.180
There's no point in having dreams until she gets her driver's license.
在拿到驾照之前，谈什么梦想都没意义。

1698
01:30:08.080 --> 01:30:09.940
That's going to change your life.
那会改变你的生活。

1699
01:30:10.240 --> 01:30:10.520
Yeah.
是啊。

1700
01:30:11.220 --> 01:30:11.980
All right.
好吧。

1701
01:30:11.980 --> 01:30:13.040
Last question.
最后一个问题。

1702
01:30:13.400 --> 01:30:15.840
What is your favorite midnight snack?
你最喜欢的宵夜是什么？

1703
01:30:16.520 --> 01:30:17.460
Oh, man.
天哪。

1704
01:30:17.620 --> 01:30:17.940
I juSt.
我只是。

1705
01:30:18.120 --> 01:30:18.500
Okay.
好吧。

1706
01:30:18.700 --> 01:30:30.760
So Paul Lieberstein, his son, had a recipe that they shared with me when he was in first
保罗·利伯斯坦（Paul Lieberstein）的儿子，他在一年级的时候，

1707
01:30:30.760 --> 01:30:31.120
grade.
他们跟我分享了一个食谱。

1708
01:30:31.600 --> 01:30:33.880
It's the easiest thing to make in the world.
那是世界上最简单的做法。

1709
01:30:34.120 --> 01:30:38.200
It's Greek yogurt and self-rising flour mixed.
就是希腊酸奶和自发粉混合。

1710
01:30:38.480 --> 01:30:39.860
And it becomes a dough.
然后它就变成了面团。

1711
01:30:40.440 --> 01:30:42.460
And you can then bake it.
你可以把它烤了。

1712
01:30:42.620 --> 01:30:44.580
And you can make a bagel out of it.
你可以用它做贝果。

1713
01:30:44.660 --> 01:30:45.960
You can make a biscuit out of it.
你可以用它做饼干。

1714
01:30:46.060 --> 01:30:47.760
It's like a good dough.
这是一种很好的面团。

1715
01:30:48.040 --> 01:30:54.380
And so what I've been doing lately is putting different things inside of it and making like.
所以我最近一直在做的是，在里面放各种东西，做成那种。

1716
01:30:54.580 --> 01:30:56.420
A little bread pocket of goodness.
美味的小面包口袋。

1717
01:30:56.420 --> 01:30:57.620
Yeah, like a little hot pocket.
对，就像小热狗包一样。

1718
01:30:57.820 --> 01:30:58.960
Like what do you put inside it?
你会在里面放什么？

1719
01:30:58.960 --> 01:30:59.580
And putting it in the toaster oven.
然后把它放进烤箱里。

1720
01:30:59.940 --> 01:31:04.320
I put in some chicken and onions in the middle of the night, the other night.
前几天半夜，我往里面放了些鸡肉和洋葱。

1721
01:31:05.460 --> 01:31:08.760
You whip up a from scratch dough.
你居然现做面团。

1722
01:31:09.360 --> 01:31:10.060
It's not.
并不是。

1723
01:31:10.120 --> 01:31:10.660
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1724
01:31:10.660 --> 01:31:11.180
Very nice.
真不错。

1725
01:31:11.300 --> 01:31:12.400
That sounds really good.
听起来真的很棒。

1726
01:31:12.540 --> 01:31:12.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1727
01:31:13.200 --> 01:31:13.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1728
01:31:14.000 --> 01:31:16.300
I'm going to hit you up for that recipe, actually.
说真的，我回头得找你要那个食谱。

1729
01:31:16.520 --> 01:31:17.300
Oh, you just heard it.
哦，你刚才不就听到了吗。

1730
01:31:17.380 --> 01:31:18.460
There's nothing new.
没什么新鲜的。

1731
01:31:18.460 --> 01:31:19.540
But what are the proportions?
但比例是多少呢？

1732
01:31:19.940 --> 01:31:20.360
Is it like.
是那种。

1733
01:31:20.360 --> 01:31:20.800
50-50.
五五开吗。

1734
01:31:21.120 --> 01:31:23.340
Oh, so a cup of dough and a cup of yogurt.
哦，所以是一杯面粉加一杯酸奶。

1735
01:31:23.460 --> 01:31:25.180
Like cup of yogurt, cup of flour.
就像一杯酸奶，一杯面粉。

1736
01:31:25.560 --> 01:31:25.780
Right.
对。

1737
01:31:25.940 --> 01:31:27.160
Cup of flour, cup of yogurt.
一杯面粉，一杯酸奶。

1738
01:31:27.460 --> 01:31:33.380
And to keep it to two ingredients, it's self-rising flour, which is basically flour that already has baking powder mixed into it.
为了保持只有两种配料，要用自发粉，也就是已经混入了泡打粉的面粉。

1739
01:31:33.460 --> 01:31:33.680
Sure.
当然。

1740
01:31:33.740 --> 01:31:37.140
But you could just put in a teaspoon of baking powder to a cup of flour.
但你也可以直接往一杯面粉里加一茶匙泡打粉。

1741
01:31:37.260 --> 01:31:38.360
And then you knead it up.
然后把它揉匀。

1742
01:31:38.700 --> 01:31:40.700
And then you can just put something in it.
接着你就可以往里面加点东西了。

1743
01:31:40.700 --> 01:31:46.240
And you press it into the tray that comes with the toaster oven.
把它压进烤箱自带的托盘里。

1744
01:31:46.420 --> 01:31:48.760
And then you put whatever filling you want on top of it.
然后在上面放上你想要的任何馅料。

1745
01:31:48.820 --> 01:31:51.940
And you just kind of fold the flaps up and try and seal it up.
把边缘折起来，尽量封好。

1746
01:31:52.160 --> 01:31:53.440
How long do you bake it for?
你要烤多久？

1747
01:31:53.900 --> 01:31:54.260
I don't know.
我不知道。

1748
01:31:54.420 --> 01:31:54.980
25 minutes.
25分钟吧。

1749
01:31:55.080 --> 01:31:55.340
Doesn't matter.
无所谓。

1750
01:31:55.380 --> 01:31:56.660
You can't really overbake it that much.
反正也烤不坏。

1751
01:31:56.800 --> 01:31:57.920
It just gets a little crustier.
它只是变得稍微硬了一些。

1752
01:31:58.700 --> 01:32:00.400
It's not like exact science.
这又不是什么精确科学。

1753
01:32:00.660 --> 01:32:03.660
Greg, we have asked so many people this question.
格雷格，我们问过很多人这个问题了。

1754
01:32:03.660 --> 01:32:07.860
And that is the most unique answer I've ever gotten given.
而这是我听过最独特的回答。

1755
01:32:08.600 --> 01:32:09.540
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1756
01:32:10.700 --> 01:32:13.240
So, Greg, thank you so much for coming in and marking this occasion.
所以，格雷格，非常感谢你今天能来参加这个特别的时刻。

1757
01:32:13.240 --> 01:32:14.120
Well, it's always so fun.
嗯，这总是很有趣。

1758
01:32:14.120 --> 01:32:15.200
I love your show.
我喜欢你们的节目。

1759
01:32:15.600 --> 01:32:19.920
And, you know, obviously, I'm very interested in the content of your show.
而且，你知道，显然我对你们节目的内容非常感兴趣。

1760
01:32:21.460 --> 01:32:22.600
Are we doing okay?
我们表现得还可以吗？

1761
01:32:22.780 --> 01:32:23.640
Did we get it right?
我们问对了吗？

1762
01:32:23.840 --> 01:32:24.480
It's fabulous.
太棒了。

1763
01:32:24.560 --> 01:32:27.600
You know, and you guys always do your homework so well.
你知道，你们总是把功课做得这么好。

1764
01:32:27.720 --> 01:32:29.220
And you always have such interesting questions.
而且你们总能提出这么有趣的问题。

1765
01:32:29.560 --> 01:32:34.260
And, you know, such a fun experience to come on the show and to hang out with you guys.
能来上节目和你们一起聊天，真是太愉快的体验了。

1766
01:32:34.420 --> 01:32:37.840
I miss having you in my daily life.
我怀念每天有你在身边的日子。

1767
01:32:38.080 --> 01:32:39.000
Oh, Greg.
噢，格雷格。

1768
01:32:39.460 --> 01:32:40.580
I feel the same way.
我有同感。

1769
01:32:40.580 --> 01:32:40.880
Thank you so much.
非常感谢你。

1770
01:32:41.080 --> 01:32:41.620
Thank you.
谢谢。

1771
01:32:41.880 --> 01:32:46.320
Well, you know, we so appreciate, too, the fans send in fantastic questions.
嗯，你知道，我们也特别感谢粉丝们寄来的精彩问题。

1772
01:32:46.320 --> 01:32:52.440
So, we have to, like, thank them for helping inspire us to ask you the things we do ask you.
所以，我们得感谢他们，是他们启发了我们去问你那些问题。

1773
01:32:52.580 --> 01:32:54.100
But what a joy to see you.
能见到你真是太高兴了。

1774
01:32:54.300 --> 01:32:58.800
And we can't wait to talk more about the paper with you when you're ready.
等你准备好了，我们迫不及待想和你深入聊聊这部作品。

1775
01:32:59.080 --> 01:32:59.340
Sure.
没问题。

1776
01:32:59.720 --> 01:33:01.720
Well, I can't wait for people to see it.
嗯，我也迫不及待想让大家看到它了。

1777
01:33:01.720 --> 01:33:08.820
